---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const updated = 'July 21, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — AppsAnalyzer"
  description="How AppsAnalyzer handles your data. Spoiler: everything runs locally on your device and nothing is collected."
>
  <article class="legal container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>AppsAnalyzer</strong> ("the app", "we", "us")
      handles information when you use it. AppsAnalyzer is designed to be private by default:
      all analysis happens locally on your device.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      AppsAnalyzer does <strong>not</strong> collect, transmit, or store any personal
      information on external servers. The app does not require you to create an account
      and does not use any analytics or tracking SDKs.
    </p>

    <h2>2. On-Device Data</h2>
    <p>
      To do its job, the app reads the list of applications installed on your device and
      inspects their publicly available package files (APKs) to detect the framework they
      were built with. This processing happens entirely on your device. Results may be
      cached locally (using a Room database) so the app loads faster the next time you open
      it. This cached data never leaves your device and is removed when you clear the app's
      data or uninstall it.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Permissions</h2>
    <p>
      AppsAnalyzer requests access to query the list of installed applications solely to
      analyze and categorize them. It does not access your files, contacts, messages,
      camera, microphone, or location, and it does not require root access.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      Because no data is collected or transmitted off your device, we do not sell, share, or
      disclose any personal information to third parties.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      The app itself does not integrate third-party advertising or analytics services. If
      you download the app from a distribution platform (such as a website or app store),
      that platform's own privacy policy governs any data it collects during download.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      AppsAnalyzer is not directed to children under the age of 13 and does not knowingly
      collect any information from them.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on
      this page with an updated "Last updated" date.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please open an issue on our
      <a href="https://github.com/shubham-soni9/Apps-Analyzer" rel="noopener" target="_blank">GitHub repository</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding-top: 64px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--brand);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 8px 0 32px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: 32px 0 10px;
  }
  .legal p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .legal p strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .legal a {
    color: var(--brand);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
